=== celesto computer create --help ===
Usage: celesto computer create [OPTIONS]

  Create a minimal computer; add --desktop for a Linux desktop.

Options:
  --desktop                       Create a Linux desktop computer instead of a
                                  minimal one.
  --local                         Use your machine (the default).
  --cloud                         Use Celesto Cloud.
  -n, --name TEXT                 Name for the computer.
  --os [alpine|ubuntu|windows|macos]
                                  Operating system image; auto-detected when
                                  omitted.
  --image TEXT                    S3 URI or local qcow2 image path.
  --memory MIB
  --disk-size MIB
  --width INTEGER
  --height INTEGER
  --backend [auto|firecracker|qemu|libkrun|vz]
                                  Virtualization backend.
  --qemu-machine [auto|q35|microvm]
                                  QEMU machine model.  [default: auto]
  --comm-channel [ssh|vsock]      How Celesto sends commands to the computer.
  --mount LOCAL_PATH[:COMPUTER_PATH]
                                  Share a folder from your machine; repeat to
                                  share more than one.
  --writable-mounts               Allow the computer to change shared folders.
  --clipboard / --no-clipboard    Copy and paste between this Mac and the
                                  macOS desktop (on by default). Use --no-
                                  clipboard to keep the two clipboards
                                  separate.
  --yes                           Confirm one-time macOS image preparation.
  --network [nat|bridge]          Network mode: 'nat' (default, private
                                  network) or 'bridge' (join a network bridge
                                  on your machine).
  --bridge BRIDGE                 Linux bridge to attach to (required with
                                  --network bridge).
  --boot-timeout FLOAT            Seconds to wait for the computer to be
                                  ready.  [default: 30.0]
  --json                          Output a JSON envelope.
  -h, --help                      Show this message and exit.

=== SDK cloud create request model (installed celesto 0.1.7) ===
MODEL ComputerCreateRequest fields=size_id, vcpus, ram_mb, disk_size_mb, image, template_id, template_version, network_policy, external_volume_enabled, additional_properties
Request to create a new compute VM.

Attributes:
    size_id (None | str | Unset): Named sandbox size
    vcpus (int | None | Unset): Number of virtual CPUs
    ram_mb (int | None | Unset): RAM in megabytes
    disk_size_mb (int | None | Unset): Disk size in megabytes (20 GB maximum)
    image (str | Unset):  Default: 'ubuntu-desktop-24.04'.
    template_id (None | str | Unset): Sandbox template id, e.g. scratch or coding-agent
    template_version (None | str | Unset): Optional immutable template version; latest if omitted
    network_policy (NetworkPolicy | Unset): Outbound internet access, fixed for the lifetime of a computer.
    external_volume_enabled (bool | Unset): Attach a persistent external volume at /home/ohm that survives
        stop/restore. Off by default (the sandbox is otherwise ephemeral); cannot be changed after create. Default:
        False.
MODEL ComputerPublishedPortCreateRequest fields=port, force, additional_properties
Request to publish a sandbox port to the internet.

Attributes:
    port (int | Unset): HTTP application port; Celesto system ports are reserved Default: 8000.
    force (bool | Unset): Compatibility flag; publish requests already reapply active host routes Default: False.
MODEL ComputerPublishedPortResponse fields=computer_id, port, status, id, url, created_at, additional_properties
Public route for a port inside a computer.

Attributes:
    computer_id (str):
    port (int):
    status (str):
    id (None | str | Unset):
    url (None | str | Unset):
    created_at (None | str | Unset):
MODEL NetworkPolicy fields=mode
Outbound internet access, fixed for the lifetime of a computer.

Attributes:
    mode (NetworkPolicyMode | Unset):  Default: NetworkPolicyMode.OPEN.
